  "meta": {
    "description": "Phase 5 (ADR-020): n8n fronts the backend's retrieval-grounded Q&A as an observable workflow -- query -> POST /api/chat (backend owns retrieval, prompt construction, LLM call, and citation assembly, per ADR-020's 'retrieval and business logic stay in backend services') -> response, with every call logged in n8n's execution history. Unlike 01/02, this workflow calls a public backend endpoint (no Internal API Key credential needed), so it ships active without the manual credential step those require. POST {\"question\": \"...\"} to /webhook/rag-chat; returns the same {answer, citations, model} shape as POST /api/chat directly, or a 404 with an explanatory message if nothing indexed matches (e.g. no approved documents yet) or the chat service errors."
